a 100-cell copy costs 200 (a store and a read per cell): true
equal stores over equal extents: the cheap expression costs 200, the costly one 1000: true
a 10^12-store nest saturates at the cap: true
at an Int.max_value cap the product saturates instead of wrapping: true
an empty loop costs nothing: true
a whole-node zero costs its cells: true
a guarded body is charged guards-taken (the comparison plus the store per iteration): true
a barrier is unknown work: true
a scan loop is unknown work: true
